    "_postman_id": "eaa28658-c8f9-4aeb-97f2-a5b81fdae648",
    "name": "📌 AssemblyAI API",
    "description": "### About AssemblyAI\n\n\"AI models to transcribe and understand speech\"\n\nAssemblyAI builds its own speech-to-text models, such as Universal. On the workspace overview it is listed under **Speech & audio**.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Postman Account\n    \n- AssemblyAI Account: [https://www.assemblyai.com/](https://www.assemblyai.com/)\n    \n\n### Usage\n\n1. Create a fork\n    \n2. Update collection variables\n    \n3. Send requests\n\nStart with the 🚀 Get Started folder.\n\nAdd your key to your **Postman Vault** as `assemblyai_api_key` (Vault icon in the footer, then **Add secret**, using that exact name). Requests read it as `{{vault:assemblyai_api_key}}`, so your key never leaves your device.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- API: [https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/api-reference/transcripts/submit](https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/api-reference/transcripts/submit)\n    \n- Models: [https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/select-the-speech-model](https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/pre-recorded-audio/select-the-speech-model)\n\n### Notes\n\nTranscription is asynchronous: **Speech-to-Text / Get transcript** polls `temp.transcript_id` until `status` is `completed`.",
